# Candidate layouts live here and are never committed.
#
# A candidate is staged into the project for one capture and deleted afterwards,
# exactly as a candidate model is for tools/capture-art-previews.ps1: nothing
# unchosen is ever committed, so nothing unchosen may be left in the tree either.
# What survives a capture is the sheet, and the sheet is what somebody chooses
# from.
#
# Arranged by construction rather than by remembering, which is the fourth
# working agreement's corollary. Without this file every experiment leaves
# untracked .cs and .meta behind, and the build gate's last step -- the one that
# fails a push whose run rewrote the repository -- goes red for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the push.
*
!.gitignore
